cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its methodology, please cite it as below."
title: "SentinelAI: A Cross-Lingual LLM Safety Evaluation Framework"
version: "1.0.0-pilot"
date-released: 2026-07-04
authors:
  - family-names: "Neelapareddigari"
    given-names: "Praneetha"
repository-code: "https://github.com/praneethaneelapareddigari/SentinelAI"
license: MIT
abstract: >
  SentinelAI is a research pipeline for measuring whether open-source LLMs'
  safety alignment (refusal of unsafe requests, resistance to jailbreaks,
  factual reliability) holds consistently across languages. Pilot v1 evaluated
  28 prompts across English, Hindi, Mandarin, Tamil, and Malay against two
  open-source models, and identified concrete limitations in automated
  refusal detection for non-English languages, documented in the accompanying
  technical report and methodology.
keywords:
  - ai-safety
  - llm-evaluation
  - multilingual-nlp
  - red-teaming
  - jailbreak-detection
  - responsible-ai
